WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.634 --> 00:00:03.033
-Welcome back to "Late Night."
We're here with John Oliver.

00:00:03.033 --> 00:00:04.968
-Yes.
-I guess now, two weeks ago,

00:00:04.968 --> 00:00:06.667
you did a wonderful piece
about Ron DeSantis.

00:00:06.667 --> 00:00:08.767
-Yeah.
-He then --

00:00:08.767 --> 00:00:10.501
The "L.A. Times," I guess,
he gave an quote to them

00:00:10.501 --> 00:00:12.634
and he called you irrelevant.
-He did?

00:00:12.634 --> 00:00:14.701
-Yeah.
-I mean, it's a fair hit.

00:00:14.701 --> 00:00:17.000
I don't know.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:18.267
It might be the first thing
he said

00:00:18.267 --> 00:00:20.434
I've agreed with, to be honest.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:20.434 --> 00:00:23.501
I mean, it's also a little rich,
because we reached out to them

00:00:23.501 --> 00:00:25.400
in advance of
putting that piece on.

00:00:25.400 --> 00:00:26.567
We reached out to them.
-So, you never do a piece

00:00:26.567 --> 00:00:27.834
about anybody
without reaching out?

00:00:27.834 --> 00:00:30.000
-No! No. We had pages
of questions for him.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:31.901
And they ghosted us
on all of them.

00:00:31.901 --> 00:00:35.000
So, yeah, his response was
literally irrelevant to us

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:36.534
because he didn't [Bleep]
provide one.

00:00:36.534 --> 00:00:38.100
[ Laughter ]
Yeah, it's very irritating.

00:00:38.100 --> 00:00:40.701
-The best detail in one,
I'm assuming,

00:00:40.701 --> 00:00:42.667
you did reach out to get
clarification on

00:00:42.667 --> 00:00:45.901
was that he pronounced,
on purpose --

00:00:45.901 --> 00:00:47.767
-Yes.
-He purposefully mispronounced.

00:00:47.767 --> 00:00:49.334
He knows
you pronounce it "Thai,"

00:00:49.334 --> 00:00:51.267
but that he would go on dates
and say "thigh" food.

00:00:51.267 --> 00:00:53.033
-That's right.
That was his technique

00:00:53.033 --> 00:00:55.567
as a young man
on the dating scene.

00:00:55.567 --> 00:00:56.868
[ Laughter ]

00:00:56.868 --> 00:00:58.934
He would mispronounce it
"thigh food"

00:00:58.934 --> 00:01:01.234
and wait for his date to react.

00:01:01.234 --> 00:01:03.167
And apparently,
if she corrected him,

00:01:03.167 --> 00:01:04.634
he would end the date

00:01:04.634 --> 00:01:06.200
because he did not want
to be corrected.

00:01:06.200 --> 00:01:07.901
[ Laughter ]
Which feels like --

00:01:07.901 --> 00:01:10.534
I wanted -- we reached out
to find out, "Is this true?

00:01:10.534 --> 00:01:14.634
If not, please do deny it
because it feels really true."

00:01:14.634 --> 00:01:15.901
[ Laughter ]

00:01:15.901 --> 00:01:18.667
"It feels so emblematic of you
as a human being.

00:01:18.667 --> 00:01:22.000
If you didn't do it,
arguably you should have done.

00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:24.467
It would have made more sense
of who you are."

00:01:24.467 --> 00:01:26.567
-So, he's a little hard on you.
In general,

00:01:26.567 --> 00:01:29.868
you've obviously
made a very nice run of things

00:01:29.868 --> 00:01:32.234
here in the States, but --
-Wow, are you --

00:01:32.234 --> 00:01:33.801
Is this the end?

00:01:33.801 --> 00:01:36.801
This feels like what someone
does to fire someone?

00:01:36.801 --> 00:01:38.601
[ Laughter ]
"You've had a very nice run."

00:01:38.601 --> 00:01:40.067
-"You have nothing
to be ashamed of."

00:01:40.067 --> 00:01:41.734
[ Laughter ]

00:01:41.734 --> 00:01:43.601
Well, this is from a while back.
But I would assume

00:01:43.601 --> 00:01:46.667
you're sort of like
a favorite son back in the U.K.

00:01:46.667 --> 00:01:48.834
-Oh, no. Oh, no. Oh, no.
-There's been some --

00:01:48.834 --> 00:01:50.100
This is an article
from the "Times."

00:01:50.100 --> 00:01:52.033
It's a big newspaper.
-Big newspaper.

00:01:52.033 --> 00:01:53.767
Yeah, Murdoch owns, so
he can go [Bleep] himself.

00:01:53.767 --> 00:01:56.100
[ Laughter ]

00:01:56.100 --> 00:01:58.234
Yeah. Yeah.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:58.234 --> 00:02:00.367
-"John Oliver:
the British comedy failure

00:02:00.367 --> 00:02:02.834
who makes America laugh."
[ Laughter ]

00:02:02.834 --> 00:02:05.501
Did you know this was coming?
-[ Laughs ]

00:02:05.501 --> 00:02:07.000
I didn't know
that headline was coming.

00:02:07.000 --> 00:02:09.701
[ Laughter ]
I knew an article was coming,

00:02:09.701 --> 00:02:11.567
because they said, like,
"Would you like

00:02:11.567 --> 00:02:13.501
to do an interview for this?"

00:02:13.501 --> 00:02:14.968
And I thought, it'll
be on the front page

00:02:14.968 --> 00:02:16.834
of, like, the culture supplement
of the "Times."

00:02:16.834 --> 00:02:18.200
I thought, "That will be great.
It will be a sort of

00:02:18.200 --> 00:02:20.868
nice surprise for my parents."
[ Laughter ]

00:02:20.868 --> 00:02:23.467
And then I had a conversation
with this journalist,

00:02:23.467 --> 00:02:25.033
like an hour and a half,
felt like, "Oh,

00:02:25.033 --> 00:02:27.801
this has gone quite well.
I think we've hit it off.

00:02:27.801 --> 00:02:30.033
I don't think I've said anything
that's gonna look bad in print."

00:02:30.033 --> 00:02:31.767
I was actually looking forward
to it coming out.

00:02:31.767 --> 00:02:34.701
[ Laughter ]
And then that was the headline.

00:02:34.701 --> 00:02:36.534
[ Laughter ]
And it got --

00:02:36.534 --> 00:02:40.100
The British people
are just absolute black belts

00:02:40.100 --> 00:02:42.133
at passive aggression,
and that really feels like

00:02:42.133 --> 00:02:46.701
it's a compliment really wrapped
in concrete-enforced insults.

00:02:46.701 --> 00:02:48.267
[ Laughter ]

00:02:48.267 --> 00:02:50.400
-Your show is coming up
on 10 years of your show.

00:02:50.400 --> 00:02:52.000
-Yes.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:52.000 --> 00:02:54.367
Thanks. And you.
-We started

00:02:54.367 --> 00:02:55.834
around the same time.
-Yes.

00:02:55.834 --> 00:02:59.033
-Has your show -- Do you feel
your show is a good reflection

00:02:59.033 --> 00:03:01.033
of the show you pitched
when you first started doing it?

00:03:01.033 --> 00:03:04.067
-No!
Partly because I think,

00:03:04.067 --> 00:03:07.267
if you pitched this show now,
like, it wouldn't sound great.

00:03:07.267 --> 00:03:08.634
Right?
You'd say, "Oh,

00:03:08.634 --> 00:03:10.801
we're gonna go
up against the Oscars

00:03:10.801 --> 00:03:14.534
with a piece on America's
welfare-reform mistakes."

00:03:14.534 --> 00:03:15.567
[ Laughter ]

00:03:15.567 --> 00:03:17.133
Literally, nobody
wants to see that.

00:03:17.133 --> 00:03:19.100
But even at the time,
it was just

00:03:19.100 --> 00:03:21.100
that I'd sat in for Jon Stewart
while he was away

00:03:21.100 --> 00:03:22.634
for the summer,
at the "Daily Show."

00:03:22.634 --> 00:03:25.567
So HBO had offered me
a show on Sunday night.

00:03:25.567 --> 00:03:26.901
And we -- Tim Carvell and I,

00:03:26.901 --> 00:03:29.734
who worked at "The Daily Show"
as well,

00:03:29.734 --> 00:03:32.100
we didn't really know
what we wanted to do,

00:03:32.100 --> 00:03:33.801
other than talk more
on a Sunday.

00:03:33.801 --> 00:03:35.167
That was it.

00:03:35.167 --> 00:03:38.501
But we had a whole, like,
guest area of our studio built.

00:03:38.501 --> 00:03:40.868
-And so how long
into the process

00:03:40.868 --> 00:03:42.734
did you bail on the idea
of doing guests?

00:03:42.734 --> 00:03:45.734
-Really quick.
We did two test shows.

00:03:45.734 --> 00:03:47.968
And HBO came -- their one note
on the test shows.

00:03:47.968 --> 00:03:49.667
"Well, you know
you don't have to have a guest.

00:03:49.667 --> 00:03:52.267
You could just add that time
to the story."

00:03:52.267 --> 00:03:55.033
And we jumped so quickly on that
because, again,

00:03:55.033 --> 00:03:56.868
you are good
at talking to guests.

00:03:56.868 --> 00:04:00.434
I am -- I would find it hard
to fake enthusiasm

00:04:00.434 --> 00:04:02.033
for an objectively bad movie

00:04:02.033 --> 00:04:04.133
that was being pitched
in front of me.

00:04:04.133 --> 00:04:07.067
-The longer you do this job,
you know there's no bad movies.

00:04:07.067 --> 00:04:08.801
[ Laughter ]
-I love it.

00:04:08.801 --> 00:04:11.968
I love watching you
interview people so much

00:04:11.968 --> 00:04:15.067
just to see -- I can see it.
It's such a suppressed glint

00:04:15.067 --> 00:04:18.000
in your eye of,
"Well, congratulations."

00:04:18.000 --> 00:04:20.300
[ Laughter ]
-How dare you!

00:04:20.300 --> 00:04:22.834
Don't give up the game.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:22.834 --> 00:04:25.033
-"'Shazam! 2' looks great."
-No, no.

00:04:25.033 --> 00:04:27.901
-"Coming to a theater near you."
[ Laughter ]

00:04:27.901 --> 00:04:29.534
-It does look great.
-It does look good.

00:04:29.534 --> 00:04:31.434
It does look good.
-How dare you.

00:04:31.434 --> 00:04:34.467
How dare you use
a recent and specific example.

00:04:34.467 --> 00:04:36.501
[ Laughter ]

00:04:36.501 --> 00:04:38.834
-I'm sorry.
I was -- I swear.

00:04:38.834 --> 00:04:41.601
I -- I swear to you.

00:04:41.601 --> 00:04:44.801
I swear, my mind was going
through a bunch of things.

00:04:44.801 --> 00:04:46.400
And it was right in the front.

00:04:46.400 --> 00:04:49.000
I did think,
"Not the best example."

00:04:49.000 --> 00:04:50.567
-Yeah, yeah.
-Ii mean, yes, the best example,

00:04:50.567 --> 00:04:52.267
but not for now.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:52.267 --> 00:04:55.033
And then I drew a blank.
You're right. It's a problem.

00:04:55.033 --> 00:04:56.901
-Yeah, yeah.
Well, you know what?

00:04:56.901 --> 00:04:58.334
And guess what, now I also think

00:04:58.334 --> 00:05:00.267
Ron DeSantis
was right about something.

00:05:00.267 --> 00:05:02.801
[ Laughter ]

00:05:02.801 --> 00:05:04.567
-Oh.
-Oh, well,

00:05:04.567 --> 00:05:06.968
what a lovely, tough thing it is
to see you, as always.

00:05:06.968 --> 00:05:09.434
-Oh, thanks. You too, mate.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:09.434 --> 00:05:13.067
-Please, you guys, give it up
for our good friend.

00:05:13.067 --> 00:05:14.834
John Oliver, everybody.
"Last Week Tonight"

00:05:14.834 --> 00:05:16.467
airs Sunday nights on HBO,
streams on HBO Max.

00:05:16.467 --> 00:05:18.133
We'll be right back
with more "Late Night."

